From e1a326ef6c8c6aa1572b3da3d15d4cfd78581cc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:06:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] feat(control-plane): carry W3C trace context into logs
 and errors

Requests reaching the control plane through the gateway carry a
correlation id, but the control plane only echoed it in some error
envelopes and wrote no structured logs, so a failing request could not
be followed from the gateway into the control plane.

A pure ASGI middleware now settles one correlation id (the first
non-empty X-Correlation-Id, otherwise a generated one) and one W3C
trace context per request: a single valid traceparent is kept, anything
else starts a new unsampled trace and drops tracestate. Both ids are
bound in contextvars for the duration of the request and written back
into the request headers in place, so the 500 handler, which runs
outside the middleware, reports the same ids.

Error envelopes gain an optional traceId, documented in the OpenAPI
Error schema (additive). The two route paths that minted a fresh
correlation id for their envelope now use the request's id.

main() configures the root logger from FORGEMESH_LOG_FORMAT (json by
default, or text) and FORGEMESH_LOG_LEVEL (INFO by default), refuses to
start on invalid values, and runs uvicorn with log_config=None so that
uvicorn's error and access logs share the format and carry the ids.
